    "sessionId": "6a086d6100049b642f85",
    "front": "A train wheel has a radius of 0.5 meters. If the train travels at 30 m/s, what is the angular speed of the wheel in radians per second?",
    "back": "Using the relation $v = r\\omega$, we solve for $\\omega = \\frac{v}{r} = \\frac{30}{0.5} = 60\\text{ rad/s}$. This means the wheel rotates through 60 radians (about 9.55 full revolutions) every second.",
