    "sessionId": "6a086d6100049b642f85",
    "front": "A satellite orbits Earth at a radius of 7000 km with a period of 90 minutes. What is its orbital speed in km/s?",
    "back": "First, convert the period to seconds: $T = 90 \\times 60 = 5400$ s. The circumference of the orbit is $C = 2\\pi r = 2\\pi(7000) \\approx 43,982$ km. Orbital speed is $v = \\frac{C}{T} = \\frac{43,982}{5400} \\approx 8.14$ km/s. This illustrates that satellites in low Earth orbit travel at roughly 8 km/s to maintain their circular path.",
    "confidence": 3,
