  {
    "userId": "6a06d147001a790ae1ce",
    "sessionId": "6a086d6100049b642f85",
    "front": "A circular running track has an inner radius of 50 meters and an outer radius of 55 meters. What is the area of the track itself (the ring between the two circles)?",
    "back": "The area of a circular ring is the difference between the areas of the outer and inner circles: $A = \\pi R^2 - \\pi r^2 = \\pi(R^2 - r^2) = \\pi(55^2 - 50^2) = \\pi(3025 - 2500) = 525\\pi \\approx 1649$ square meters. This is equivalent to $A = \\pi(R + r)(R - r)$, which shows the area depends on both the average radius and the width of the ring.",
    "confidence": 3,
