  {
    "userId": "6a06d147001a790ae1ce",
    "sessionId": "6a086d6100049b642f85",
    "front": "A 10 kg mass is swung in a horizontal circle of radius 2 m at a constant speed of 3 m/s. What is the centripetal force required to keep it in the circle?",
    "back": "Centripetal force is given by $F_c = \\frac{mv^2}{r}$. Plugging in the values: $F_c = \\frac{10 \\times 3^2}{2} = \\frac{10 \\times 9}{2} = 45$ N. This force must be directed toward the center of the circle at all times. For a mass on a string, the string tension provides this 45 N. If the string can only handle 40 N, it will break and the mass will fly off tangentially.",
    "confidence": 1,
