  {
    "userId": "6a06d147001a790ae1ce",
    "sessionId": "6a086d6100049b642f85",
    "front": "A pizza is cut into 12 equal slices. Each slice has an arc length of 4 inches on its curved crust. What is the radius of the pizza?",
    "back": "The arc length formula is $s = r\\theta$, where $\\theta$ is the central angle in radians. With 12 equal slices, each slice spans $\\theta = \\frac{2\\pi}{12} = \\frac{\\pi}{6}$ radians. Given $s = 4$ inches, solve for $r$: $r = \\frac{s}{\\theta} = \\frac{4}{\\pi/6} = 4 \\times \\frac{6}{\\pi} = \\frac{24}{\\pi} \\approx 7.64$ inches. The pizza diameter is about 15.3 inches. This relationship shows why larger pizzas are often cut into more slices — to keep crust sizes manageable.",
    "confidence": 3,
